Subject: OAGi IOF Membership – Opportunity to Nominate Representatives

Hi [Name],

We’re evaluating RTX’s participation as a contributing member of the Open Applications Group (OAGi) Industrial Ontologies Foundry (IOF) — a leading industry consortium developing open ontologies to enable data and model interoperability across manufacturing, supply chain, and enterprise systems.

Membership would position RTX to collaborate with peers (Boeing, Lockheed, Siemens, NIST, etc.) and contribute to standards directly aligned with our Digital Thread and Ontology initiatives.

As part of this effort, we’d like to identify representatives from each business unit who could participate in IOF working groups. Please let me know if you’d like to recommend someone from your organization or discuss potential areas of alignment.

Best regards,
Shatad Purohit


Subject: Interest in OAGi IOF Membership and Working Group Participation

Hi [Team],

We’re exploring RTX’s participation as a contributing member of the Open Applications Group (OAGi) Industrial Ontologies Foundry (IOF).

The IOF is an industry consortium advancing open ontologies for manufacturing, supply chain, and enterprise interoperability. Membership would allow RTX to collaborate with peers (Boeing, Lockheed, Siemens, NIST, etc.) and help shape standards directly relevant to our ontology and digital thread initiatives (e.g., REO, OCKMS).

We’d like to identify individuals interested in joining IOF working groups once our membership is active. Please reply if you’d like to participate or learn more.
